 * gh-1370 (owner directive 2026-11-05) tightens the gh-1353 "never block
 * the merge" semantics: the backstop is now a GATE on machine-owned
 * threads — a PR must not merge while ANY machine-owned review thread is
 * open ("merging with open machine threads is a policy violation"):
 *
 *  - >= IMPORTANT threads ride the digest path above (`defered:` to the
 *    one digest issue);
 *  - SUGESTION / NIT threads (below the gating threshold) resolve
 *    WITHOUT a fix — no digest, no ledger entry — each closed with the
 *    machine-parsed ack tag `wontfix: below gating threshold — epic
 *    invariant (gh-1370)` (reviewDispositions.TAGS; the thread must end
 *    RESOLVED);
 *  - human-owned threads stay untouched (gh-744): never machine-resolved,
 *    branch protection owns them;
 *  - ANY resolution failure (a resolve/ack API error, a partial
 *    resolution, a machine thread without a resolvable id) HOLDS the
 *    merge: runBackstop throws, the caller defers THAT merge to the next
 *    tick (the retry), and a repeat failure keeps failing the merge
 *    funnel job (the escalation surface). The unchanged failure classes:
 *    a threads/comments READ that throws through (fail-closed
 *    read — the #1319 pathology), a digest-FILING failure throws through,
 *    and a MISSING threads primitive merely skips the backstop
 *    (capability miss — nothing is visible, nothing is unresolved).
 *  - per-thread resolve/ack failures are still counted, never abort the
 *    rest of the loop (gh-828 round 3: resolve FIRST, ack only on
 *    success) — the gate throws AFTER the loop so every thread attempts
 *    each tick.
``

